- Removed the E.defrag() pause when opening Volume Adjustment. The critical menu-to-game defrag that protects CARAVAN_RENDERER remains unchanged.
- Reworked CARAVAN_AUDIO_APPLY into an asynchronous chunked worker. Large music-volume changes now process only 8 ADPCM blocks / 2048 audio bytes per event-loop turn instead of rewriting the entire 414 KB music file in one blocking callback.
- The Volume Adjustment screen remains responsive while applying and displays Applying volume... with progress.
- Turning ON/OFF no longer runs the audio apply helper because enable/disable state only needs SOUND.CFG; no WAV rewrite is required.
