- Added a BACKGROUND MUSIC section under Volume Adjustment.
- Added the Lazy Days Tired submenu with Music ON/OFF, Volume 0-15, Preview PLAY/STOP, and Back.
- Added the on-device credit: "Music by Geoff Harvey from Pixabay"; full linked attribution is included in README.md.
- Added the supplied LAZY_DAYS_TIRED.WAV as a streamed 16 kHz mono WAV asset.
- Background music starts only after the Caravan board/renderer has loaded and loops natively while the game is active.
- Card-play/discard effects temporarily take the audio channel; when each short effect finishes, Lazy Days Tired restarts and continues looping if Background Music is enabled.
- SOUND.CFG expanded from 4 to 6 characters to store music ON/OFF and volume while remaining backward-compatible with existing 4-character settings.
- Background Music defaults ON at volume 10; maximum remains 15.
- Existing card sound menus, louder WAVs, gameplay, results animation, and low-memory game-start path are preserved.

0.5.30 - 2026-09-09
- Rebased game startup and renderer loading on the known-working v0.5.22/v0.5.18 architecture after v0.5.29 reached YOUR TURN but never drew the actual board.
- Removed the entire resident gameplay sound engine and SOUND.JSON object from APP memory.
- Volume Adjustment is now a self-contained module that exists only while that menu is open and is fully removed before game launch.
- Sound settings are stored in a tiny 4-character SOUND.CFG file instead of keeping a config object alive in APP.
- CARAVAN_GAME does not load or parse sound settings during startup. The 4-byte config is read only when a card is actually played/discarded.
- Gameplay WAV playback is direct from CARAVAN_GAME with no separate CARAVAN_SFX runtime module.
- Game startup unloads the sound menu, defragments, waits 50 ms for the menu event to unwind, defragments again, then loads the proven CARAVAN_GAME.MIN.JS.
- Playing Card / Discard ON-OFF, 0-15 volume, PLAY/STOP preview, louder WAVs, and the Pixabay credit remain.

0.5.22 - 2026-09-09
- Replaced the sound preview helper text in both Playing Card and Discard sound menus with:
  "Sound Effect by Alex from Pixabay"
- No sound playback, volume, preview, gameplay, or animation behavior changed.

0.5.21 - 2026-09-09
- Increased the maximum audible level of both Caravan card sound effects without changing the 0-15 menu range or preview controls.
- Peak-normalized CARD_PLAY.WAV and CARD_DISCARD.WAV to approximately -1.5 dBFS, preserving 16 kHz mono 16-bit PCM streaming and avoiding clipping.
- Playing Card received about +15.2 dB of source gain; Discard received about +9.8 dB so both effects reach a much stronger maximum at Volume 15.
- No gameplay logic, sound-menu behavior, preview timing, bottle-cap results animation, or low-memory architecture was changed.

0.5.20 - 2026-09-09
- Added a Preview: PLAY / Preview: STOP row inside both Playing Card and Discard sound submenus.
- Preview streams the selected WAV at the currently selected per-effect volume so volume can be tested directly in the settings menu.
- Preview is available even when the in-game Sound toggle is OFF; the ON/OFF toggle still controls whether the effect plays during actual Caravan gameplay.
- Preview playback can be stopped immediately, restores the Pip-Boy master volume, and is automatically stopped when leaving the submenu or Volume Adjustment menu.
- Kept the existing card-play/discard WAV files, low-memory streaming design, gameplay sound triggers, and v0.5.18 results animation unchanged.

0.5.19 - 2026-09-09
- Added the supplied Playing Card.wav for successful player/CPU card plays and Discard.wav for player/CPU discards.
- Added a new Volume Adjustment item to the first Caravan menu.
- Added a low-memory CARAVAN_SOUND.JS settings module with a SOUND EFFECTS menu and highlighted Playing Card / Discard submenus.
- Added independent Sound ON/OFF toggles and 0-15 volume adjustment for each effect; settings persist in HOLO/CARAVAN/SOUND.JSON.
- Sound volume is applied relative to the Pip-Boy master volume and restored after each short effect.
- Streamed WAV playback avoids preloading audio buffers into RAM.
- Kept the v0.5.18 bottle-cap results animation, 12 FPS timing, layout, and low-memory CAP.IMG path unchanged.

0.5.18 - 2026-09-09
- Replaced the results-animation bottle-cap artwork with the newly supplied IMAGE (1)(2).IMG source.
- Kept the exact 12 FPS cap pop/pulse, counter, CAPS bounce/fade, and overall animation timing from v0.5.17.
- Shifted the cap 22 px toward screen center and shifted the animated +/- counter 5 px toward center so the widget reads as one tighter group.
- Shifted the entire CAPS label animation 22 px upward and 5 px left so CAPS sits much closer to the animated +/- amount while preserving the same drop/bounce trajectory.
- Preserved the v0.5.17 low-memory design: one 1,804-byte runtime CAP.IMG loaded only for the results widget.
- Preserved the newly supplied cap image byte-for-byte as CAP_SOURCE.IMG in the source package.

0.5.17 - 2026-09-09
- Fixed a LOW_MEMORY/MEMORY crash observed immediately after Ringo won and the results animation began.
- Deferred results-animation startup by 100 ms so the finished CARAVAN_GAME timer callback can fully unwind before the results module is loaded and memory is defragmented.
- Replaced the 11,899-byte CAP_ANIM.BIN runtime buffer with one 1,804-byte transparent CAP.IMG.
- The single 120x120 cap image is scaled at draw time for the 96/108/114/120 pop states and uses display intensity for the fade, preserving the 12 FPS timeline while sharply reducing peak RAM.
- Kept the supplied CAP_SOURCE.IMG unchanged in the source package.

0.5.16 - 2026-09-09
- Replaced the results-animation bottle-cap artwork with the newly supplied IMAGE (2).IMG source.
- Kept the 12 FPS results timing, win/loss layout, and fast 0 -> +/-ante counter behavior from v0.5.15.
- Merged all eight pre-scaled/fade cap runtime images into one CAP_ANIM.BIN file, reducing the cap animation from eight device files to one.
- Preserved the supplied cap source byte-for-byte as CAP_SOURCE.IMG in the package source tree; runtime conversion remains transparent 1-bit for low-memory Pip-Boy drawing.
- Runtime slices only the needed packed frame when the cap state changes and releases the packed buffer when the results module closes.

0.5.15 - 2026-09-09
- Retimed the results cap animation for the Pip-Boy's 12 FPS target. The supplied 480x320 reference AVI was inspected only for frame-rate/display timing and is not included or played by the holotape.
- Preserved the original ~3.7 second HUDCaps-style timeline by sampling the 30 FPS source timeline at 12 FPS instead of stretching all 112 source frames to ~9.3 seconds.
- Moved YOU WIN / RINGO WINS / YOU LOSE above the cap animation.
- Removed all static cap-win/loss amounts from the result text. The animated cap widget is now the only place that displays the changing +caps / -caps amount.
- Kept the fast 0 -> +ante and 0 -> -ante counter animation synchronized to the sampled timeline.

0.5.14 - 2026-09-09
- Added a HUDCaps-style results animation using the supplied Nuka-Cola cap image.
- Recreated the supplied HUDCaps SWF timeline timing: 112 frames at ~30 FPS with icon pop/pulse, counter slide/bounce, CAPS drop/bounce, hold, and fade-out.
- Winning results count rapidly from 0 up to +ante caps; losing results count rapidly from 0 down to -ante caps.
- Loss results now show RINGO WINS, YOU LOSE, and the negative cap amount.
- Moved the result/menu content lower to leave the center of the 480x320 screen open for the animation.
- Added a separate CARAVAN_RESULTS.JS runtime module so the animation is loaded only after the match engine is unloaded.
- Added pre-scaled/dithered 1-bit cap assets to avoid expensive runtime image scaling and alpha work on Pip-Boy hardware.

0.5.13 - 2026-09-08
- Added full 54-card decks for both player and CPU: all 52 standard cards plus two Jokers.
- Aces are guaranteed and count as 1.
- Joker on Ace removes other numeric cards of that suit from both boards.
- Joker on 2-10 removes other cards of that rank from both boards.
- Kept J / Q / K support and updated CPU scoring for Jokers.
- Opening caravan cards are forced to numeric cards.
- Replaced per-pixel suit drawing with cached 12x12 `.IMG` suit assets.
- Initial board renders before CPU module lazy-loads.
- Removed the redundant full-board draw before the CPU turn.
- Preserved staged Demo rendering and partial selection redraws.

0.5.0
- Added Jack, Queen, and King cards to the prototype rule engine.
- Expanded card rendering for face-card ranks.

0.4.8
- Staged Demo board/hint rendering to reduce watchdog risk.
- Blocked tutorial input while a staged render is incomplete.

